  "notes": "USB 2.0 is a wire-level protocol + device-framework spec. There is no host-controller register map in this document (those live in companion specs: OHCI, UHCI, EHCI). What this document DOES specify is the standard control-transfer request layout (bmRequestType / bRequest / wValue / wIndex / wLength) and the standard descriptor types — these are universal across every USB-IF compliant device.",
  "device_request_layout": {
